Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 00:00:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Build Phase 1 cost management application shell

### Motivation
- Provide a compact, modern enterprise application shell that establishes navigation, context and responsive workspace patterns for the project controls UI.
- Deliver collapsible global and contextual sidebars, a compact top header with Enterprise and Project selectors, and a permission-aware navigation structure as the scaffolding for future module screens.
- Support very wide data workspaces with a maximum-workspace (focus) mode and responsive mobile behavior while deferring detailed data screens and Supabase/schema changes to later phases.

### Description
- Replace the starter index with a client-side application shell in `app/page.tsx` that implements modules/menus, route-aware active state, SVG icon set, `GlobalSidebar`, `ContextSidebar`, `Header`, `Dashboard` preview and `WorkspacePlaceholder` components.
- Add a catch-all route proxy `app/[...slug]/page.tsx` to allow direct addressing of module/context paths.
- Introduce a full design system stylesheet in `app/globals.css` with responsive rules, reduced-motion support, and workspace/table layout helpers.
- Update `app/layout.tsx` metadata and remove build-time remote Google Font usage by switching to local/system font fallbacks so production builds do not attempt external font fetches.

### Testing
- Ran `npm run lint` and resolved the reported hook usage issue, resulting in a clean lint pass.
- Ran `npm run build` and verified a successful production build (Next.js/Turbopack static generation completed).
- Ran `git diff --check` to validate no whitespace/format issues were introduced and confirmed working tree status post-change.
